# Route Top Loader

Use the thin fixed top progress bar for **global navigation and network feedback** across the app (public + all panels).

## Component

- `@/components/loaders/route-top-loader` → `RouteTopLoader`
- Session engine: `@/lib/loaders/global-top-loader-session` (`start` / `end` / `trackAsync`)
- Browser bindings: `@/lib/loaders/bind-global-top-loader`

## When

- Mounted **once** in `app/layout.tsx` inside `<Suspense>` — do **not** add per-page or per-panel instances.
- Activates automatically for:
  - Same-origin route navigations (links, `router.push` / `replace`, back/forward)
  - App Router RSC fetches including `router.refresh()`
  - Server actions (`Next-Action` requests)
  - URL / search-param changes that trigger network work
- Pure client-side UI stays silent: opening modals, dropdowns, accordions, tabs with cached content, client-only table filters.

## Progress behavior

- Optional short delay (~150 ms) before show (avoids flash on instant work).
- Jump to ~15–20%, trickle with easing toward ~90–95% while work is pending.
- Never hit 100% until **all** overlapping tracked ops finish.
- Then animate to 100%, hold briefly, fade out, reset.

## Forms / mutations

- **Also** keep `InlineSpinner` on submit buttons for in-form pending feedback.
- Top bar covers the global wait; spinner covers the control the user pressed.

## Do not

- Mount a second instance inside `PanelShell` or feature layouts.
- Replace `loading.tsx` with this bar — they serve different purposes (instant segment fallback vs. global progress).
- Call `toast` / sonner for navigation feedback — use this loader instead.

## Related

- Segment loading fallbacks: `@/components/loaders/route-loading` in `loading.tsx` files.
- Panel content spinner: `@/components/loaders/panel-route-loading` under role panel routes.
- Manual rare cases: `globalTopLoaderSession.trackAsync(promise)`.
